<title>DENMARK: Landesbank Schleswig-Holstein offers 4 pct bond.</title>
<headline>Landesbank Schleswig-Holstein offers 4 pct bond.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Danish lead manager BG Bank said on Monday it was arranging for Germany's Landesbank Schleswig-Holstein Zentrale (LB-Kiel) a 200 million crown, four percent, six year bond.</p>
<p>BORROWER - LANDESBANK SCHLESWIG-HOLSTEIN ZENTRALE (LB-KIEL)</p>
<p>AMT - 200 MILLION DANISH CROWNS</p>
<p>COUPON - FOUR PERCENT</p>
<p>MATURITY 27 DECEMBER 2002</p>
<p>LAST MOODY'S P-1/AA1; IBCA A1+/AAA</p>
<p>- TO BE LISTED ON COPENHAGEN STOCK EXCHANGE- NO DATE GIVEN</p>
<p>--Chris Follett, Copenhagen newsroom +45-33969652</p>
</text>
